{% comment %}
How to create the Vanta application sbomify connects with, above the
credentials form.

Written for a workspace admin who has never opened Vanta's Developer Console.
Three things decide whether a first attempt works, so each one is said where
it is needed rather than in a paragraph nobody reads:

- **Where to go.** The console lives on the account's regional app host, so
  there is one link per region. The API is the same host for all three, which
  is why nothing else on this form asks about region.
- **Which type to pick.** Developer Console offers Build Integrations first,
  its client ID and secret look exactly like a Manage Vanta one, and Vanta
  accepts them. Only the read is refused, so the warning sits on that step.
- **That the secret is shown once.** Losing it means generating another.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-text m-0">Connect your Vanta account</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">
            sbomify reads Vanta through an application you create in your own Vanta account. It takes about two minutes, and you need to be an admin in Vanta.
        </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="flex flex-col gap-3 list-decimal pl-5 text-sm text-text m-0">
        <li>
            Open the Developer Console in Vanta. Pick the one for your account:
            <span class="inline-flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-1 mt-1">
                <a href="https://app.vanta.com/settings/developer-console"
                   target="_blank"
                   rel="noopener"
                   class="font-medium">US</a>
                <a href="https://app.eu.vanta.com/settings/developer-console"
                   target="_blank"
                   rel="noopener"
                   class="font-medium">EU</a>
                <a href="https://app.aus.vanta.com/settings/developer-console"
                   target="_blank"
                   rel="noopener"
                   class="font-medium">Australia</a>
            </span>
            <span class="block text-text-muted mt-1">In Vanta this is Settings, then Developer Console.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
            Click <strong>Create</strong> and choose <strong>Manage Vanta</strong> as the application type.
            <c-feedback.alert variant="warning" class="mt-2" title="Choose Manage Vanta, not Build Integrations">
            A Build Integrations application gives you a client ID and secret that look the same, but it cannot read your frameworks or controls, so connecting fails.
            </c-feedback.alert>
        </li>
        <li>
            Give it a name you will recognise, such as <strong>sbomify Trust Center</strong>. Any description works.
        </li>
        <li>
            Click <strong>Generate client secret</strong>, then copy the client ID and the secret into the fields below. Vanta only shows the secret once.
        </li>
    </ol>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1 m-0 pl-0 list-none text-sm text-text-muted">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <i class="fas fa-lock mt-1 text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span>sbomify only asks for read access. It never changes anything in Vanta.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <i class="fas fa-circle-info mt-1 text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span>Use this application for sbomify only. Vanta keeps one active token per application, so sharing it with another tool disconnects one of them.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <i class="fas fa-eye-slash mt-1 text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span>Nothing goes on your Trust Center until you choose which frameworks to show.</span>
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>
